The Offices of Gokan

00:13:08.010 --> 00:13:09.560
We've arrived.

00:13:12.020 --> 00:13:15.060
This is the sixth court, the Offices of Henjo.

00:13:17.270 --> 00:13:19.400
Thank you for inviting me here!

00:13:19.940 --> 00:13:21.610
I've been wanting to visit this place.

00:13:21.940 --> 00:13:24.950
It's quite a mishmash of a building, isn't it?

00:13:25.990 --> 00:13:29.240
Anyway, why are you interested in this place, Lilith?

00:13:29.910 --> 00:13:31.540
Oh? You don't know?

00:13:31.830 --> 00:13:34.660
This is a Japanese mechanical mansion, you see.

00:13:35.330 --> 00:13:38.540
Lilith, you always seem to know things I don't, huh?

00:13:39.250 --> 00:13:40.840
Where do you get your info?

00:13:42.630 --> 00:13:46.090
The Iron Ball District, which we just passed through,
is also mechanical.

00:13:46.880 --> 00:13:51.560
Lord Henjo is a very innovative man
and he really loves mechanical contraptions.

00:13:52.310 --> 00:13:55.560
He also enjoys close ties with
the Offices of Enma's Engineering Department.

00:14:04.610 --> 00:14:06.280
HENJO

00:14:42.900 --> 00:14:46.990
Hmph! Things here may be mechanized,
but they're not automated.

00:14:46.990 --> 00:14:51.370
Of course they aren't.
It's still the work of Hell minions to operate them.

00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:56.120
The aides here must be knowledgeable
about mechanics, huh?

00:14:57.040 --> 00:15:00.330
I was actually planning for us all
to observe one such aide.

00:15:01.630 --> 00:15:02.710
She's right over there.

00:15:07.130 --> 00:15:11.260
Huh?! Is that aide a mechanical doll?!

00:15:11.260 --> 00:15:12.760
She's still in the prototype stage.

00:15:14.470 --> 00:15:16.180
Hi, Mr. Hozuki!

00:15:18.770 --> 00:15:20.730
This man is Lord Henjo.

00:15:20.890 --> 00:15:26.020
And this man, Horokusai, is the developer of that
mechanical doll and the current chief of staff here.

00:15:26.360 --> 00:15:31.660
Ho ha... Hofu hehihefu ha ho ho...

00:15:31.780 --> 00:15:34.280
Gramps, come on, you've got to put in your dentures.

00:15:34.620 --> 00:15:36.200
Is he alright?

00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:38.500
Horokusenile?

00:15:41.080 --> 00:15:43.290
HE'S ASKING YOU IF YOU'RE ALRIGHT, OKAY?!

00:15:43.290 --> 00:15:45.130
CERTAINLY SEEMS THAT YOU'RE NOT!

00:15:45.420 --> 00:15:48.960
Ah... Yes, yes...

00:15:48.960 --> 00:15:55.510
Lately, the records of the dead have become
quite expansive, and I can't remember them all.

00:15:55.850 --> 00:15:58.310
So I made this girl here.

00:15:58.640 --> 00:16:01.640
Rather than the amount of records,
isn't the issue that you've gotten old?

00:16:02.850 --> 00:16:10.860
This girl learns by accumulating data related
to the dead and their court proceedings...

00:16:10.860 --> 00:16:17.200
so I plan for her to eventually be able
to make extremely apt judgments in court.

00:16:18.160 --> 00:16:20.410
Her name is Memeko.

00:16:21.500 --> 00:16:26.790
I tried giving her a cute appearance so that the dead
would be less likely to get irritated by her.

00:16:27.590 --> 00:16:30.420
That kind of thing is actually quite important, isn't it?

00:16:30.840 --> 00:16:33.340
I modeled her off my own granddaughter.

00:16:33.340 --> 00:16:34.590
Oh, how cute!

00:16:34.890 --> 00:16:40.390
Pretty great, isn't she? As of now,
she's one of a kind in the whole world.

00:16:45.270 --> 00:16:47.860
Naturally, I'm the one who issues the verdicts,

00:16:48.360 --> 00:16:52.110
but a system that can instantaneously decide
where the dead should go

00:16:52.110 --> 00:16:54.530
will change even the timing
of one's second death anniversary...

00:16:54.530 --> 00:16:55.450
You okay?

00:16:55.450 --> 00:16:57.070
I do believe...

00:16:58.410 --> 00:17:05.210
Within 100 years, I truly do intend to inaugurate
the first mechanical chief of staff here at my Offices.

00:17:05.960 --> 00:17:09.420
My worry is that the geezer
you've got now won't last that long.

00:17:09.710 --> 00:17:13.590
How wonderful. Lord Henjo,
you're just like that Jobs guy.

00:17:13.880 --> 00:17:16.800
At the Offices of Enma,
we'd like to draw on your experiences here...

00:17:16.800 --> 00:17:20.720
but trying the same thing at the Offices of Enma
anytime soon, would be quite difficult.

00:17:20.720 --> 00:17:21.890
Why's that?

00:17:22.430 --> 00:17:25.560
Doing so would be no match for skilled Hell minions,

00:17:26.810 --> 00:17:31.020
and people from Mr. Hageito on down -
particularly those in the Records Department -

00:17:31.020 --> 00:17:33.940
are highly skeptical of automation.

00:17:34.490 --> 00:17:38.780
Certainly, there are some valid worries
about introducing across-the-board mechanization.

00:17:39.200 --> 00:17:43.250
Nevertheless, there's a good deal of meaning
in the way the Offices of Henjo does things.

00:17:44.450 --> 00:17:48.130
The Offices of Henjo have a replica of the Johari Mirror.

00:17:48.960 --> 00:17:51.420
They use it to interrogate the dead for a second time.

00:17:52.300 --> 00:17:56.970
The Offices of Henjo alone
have been successful in producing a replica.

00:17:57.470 --> 00:18:00.100
It'd be nice if each of the Offices could have one...

00:18:00.800 --> 00:18:03.270
But we simply don't have the materials.

00:18:03.850 --> 00:18:07.060
We created a number of prototypes
based on a rare artifact called the Shoma Mirror,

00:18:07.060 --> 00:18:10.440
and now we can't make any more of these.

00:18:10.730 --> 00:18:12.070
"The Shoma Mirror"?

00:18:12.400 --> 00:18:15.690
It's a supernatural mirror that shows
the true identifies of people and yokai.

00:18:21.830 --> 00:18:24.240
You hold it like this,

00:18:24.240 --> 00:18:28.540
and mostly check to make sure the bereaved family
back in the Mundane World is holding memorial services.

00:18:28.710 --> 00:18:31.130
Don't hold trials as if you're fixing up your makeup!

00:18:32.500 --> 00:18:34.840
You know, I'd like to see a trial.

00:18:34.840 --> 00:18:39.220
Ah, good point. I'd also like to see Memeko
do a test run, so...

00:18:40.220 --> 00:18:41.260
Beelzebub.

00:18:41.260 --> 00:18:42.050
Hm?

00:18:42.600 --> 00:18:44.100
Please play the part of the deceased.

00:18:44.100 --> 00:18:45.220
Why me?!

00:18:45.890 --> 00:18:50.900
First, the deceased's data is retrieved from Memeko,

00:18:50.900 --> 00:18:53.730
and then I read the nature of their offences out loud.

00:18:54.110 --> 00:19:00.490
In the future, I plan to have her become able to
read aloud and do everything else on her own, however.

00:19:01.070 --> 00:19:06.290
Right now, we can't do a thing
without first inputting your data.

00:19:07.120 --> 00:19:08.000
I refuse!

00:19:08.540 --> 00:19:13.880
For the sake of argument, let's say he's guilty
of tricking others and leading them down the path to evil,

00:19:14.130 --> 00:19:17.550
haughtily looks down on people,
and is quick to lose his temper.

00:19:20.720 --> 00:19:24.300
My judgment is that the Realm of Extreme Suffering
would be a good place for him.

00:19:24.550 --> 00:19:27.100
Don't shoehorn me into somewhere
in Japanese Hell like that!

00:19:27.310 --> 00:19:29.810
Oh, that's a rather apt sentence.

00:19:32.060 --> 00:19:34.520
How ludicrous. I won't stand for this!

00:19:34.520 --> 00:19:40.150
Ah, this is perfect. You see,
when the deceased tries to escape like that...

00:19:59.010 --> 00:20:01.260
Why the heck does she have that functionality?!

00:20:03.640 --> 00:20:08.390
Similarly to Lord Godotenrin's chief of staff, Miss Chun,

00:20:08.560 --> 00:20:15.020
I wanted Memeko to be able capture those deceased
who try to run away, so I based her on a cursed doll.

00:20:15.810 --> 00:20:21.450
You had some nerve to think of using your own
granddaughter as a model for this crazed doll.

00:20:22.030 --> 00:20:26.280
No matter the era, scientists are always like that!

00:20:32.710 --> 00:20:36.290
The mind she possesses is a cursed one,

00:20:36.540 --> 00:20:39.960
so I was readily able
to build artificial intelligence into her.

00:20:40.260 --> 00:20:44.590
Know what the number one thing
you shouldn't give AI to is? A cursed doll, okay?!

00:20:45.340 --> 00:20:49.220
You also shouldn't inflict excessive trauma on the dead...

00:20:49.680 --> 00:20:53.810
If you don't run away,
she's nothing more than a cute doll, after all.

00:20:54.310 --> 00:20:57.560
Mass production of more isn't really possible.

00:20:57.560 --> 00:21:02.400
There simply aren't that
many good-quality cursed dolls, you see.

00:21:02.400 --> 00:21:04.240
Oh, there, there.
I'll be damned if there were!

00:21:04.240 --> 00:21:04.990
Oh, there, there.

00:21:05.910 --> 00:21:09.530
Seems that providing
my collection to you was worthwhile.

00:21:09.530 --> 00:21:12.160
Your collection made up the raw materials?!

00:21:12.370 --> 00:21:13.120
Yeah...

00:21:13.410 --> 00:21:18.590
It was an antique doll I received from Lady Lilith
that would brandish an ice pick and chase after you.

00:21:18.960 --> 00:21:20.920
I'm glad it proved useful.

00:21:21.300 --> 00:21:23.220
Our cursed doll, you say?!

00:21:23.720 --> 00:21:26.550
Which is exactly why I invited Lady Lilith here.

00:21:26.970 --> 00:21:28.640
Should've told me that from the start...

00:21:28.970 --> 00:21:34.600
Huh? Ah... Don't Westerners like surprises?

00:21:34.770 --> 00:21:36.600
That sounds incredibly forced!

00:21:36.850 --> 00:21:40.230
Isn't the truth that you simply forgot to tell me?!

00:21:42.150 --> 00:21:45.450
So Japan has maid robots
that are able to move around, huh?

00:21:46.990 --> 00:21:48.370
That's good stuff.

00:21:49.450 --> 00:21:51.030
I'd like some, too.

00:22:05.010 --> 00:22:10.760
Uso yo. Janakya naze koko ni tadoritsuku no?
That's a lie. If not, why do you find your way here?

00:22:11.260 --> 00:22:17.350
Enma-sama no mae de nao shira o kiru no ne
Even in front of Lord Enma, you feign ignorance

00:22:17.810 --> 00:22:23.280
Baka ne. Dakedo sonna toko tamaranakute
You're an idiot. But I can't get enough of that aspect of you

00:22:24.030 --> 00:22:29.660
Teitaraku. Onaji tsumi kasanetsuzuketa
What a predicament. You continued to repeat the same sin

00:22:30.320 --> 00:22:34.950
Ii no? Yubikiri genman.
Is that alright? Pinky swear.

00:22:34.950 --> 00:22:36.330
(E?)
(Huh?)
Ii no? Yubikiri genman.
Is that alright? Pinky swear.

00:22:36.830 --> 00:22:41.170
Gachi ni honto ni naru yo.
It will seriously become reality.

00:22:41.170 --> 00:22:42.750
(Dogii!)
(Startling!)

00:22:41.170 --> 00:22:42.750
Gachi ni honto ni naru yo.
It will seriously become reality.

00:22:43.130 --> 00:22:49.130
Tensei o matazu shounetsu no mama ni
Without waiting for reincarnation, while still in the scorching heat

00:22:49.130 --> 00:22:55.180
Asa hiru eien ai o kushizashi narabete
Morning, midday, and eternally skewer desires and line them up

00:22:55.430 --> 00:22:58.350
Gutsu gutsu mou! Nie nie da yo
Already simmering! It's boiling

00:22:58.600 --> 00:23:01.770
Yuuge wa jigoku de hot pot
Supper is a hot pot in Hell

00:23:01.940 --> 00:23:07.990
Nita mono doushi ni oniai no oshioki
For people who are alike, a suitable punishment

00:23:08.150 --> 00:23:11.110
Juu juu achi! Koge koge da yo
Sizzling hot! It's burned to a crisp

00:23:11.320 --> 00:23:14.410
Anata to jigoku de hotcake
Hotcakes with you in Hell

00:23:14.580 --> 00:23:19.830
Tokoyo no suna ni naru made
Until they become forever-unchanging sand

00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:26.800
NEXT TIME
ON HOZUKI'S
COOLHEADEDNESS...

00:23:25.340 --> 00:23:29.550
Great King Enma, I'll be going to a singles party tonight,
so please allow me to leave work on time.

00:23:27.760 --> 00:23:28.340
AND

00:23:29.300 --> 00:23:29.880
BUT

00:23:29.550 --> 00:23:33.010
Oh! You're finally talking
about something amorous, Hozuki!

00:23:33.140 --> 00:23:34.760
I'm only going so that
there's an even number of guys and girls.

00:23:33.510 --> 00:23:34.350
SO

00:23:34.760 --> 00:23:36.260
So what kind of girls will be there?

00:23:36.260 --> 00:23:37.600
They're all rabbits.

00:23:36.470 --> 00:23:39.730
WE PRESENT:
THE RABBIT CALLED MUSTARD
AND
TYPES
PLEASE ENJOY!

00:23:37.600 --> 00:23:39.270
You've got a wide range of types!
